<h2>The case in brief</h2>
<p>The Director of Civil Aviation challenged, under Section 34 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, an arbitral award dated 28 April 2022 which had partly allowed Claim No. 1 in favour of the respondent contractor. When the petition reached hearing before Justice Om Prakash Shukla, the contest had narrowed to a shared position: both parties agreed that the award could be set aside and the claim sent back for fresh adjudication. The Court recorded the consent, set the award aside, and — rather than leaving the parties to begin appointment proceedings from scratch — appointed a sole arbitrator in the same order.</p>

<h2>What the order provided</h2>
<table class="law">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Direction</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
  </thead>
